"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e69a044a43cbb74ff27165978d6f708ffac3fd79c480c8534c66647e8f0d01ea", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:054fd8d08e2bdbc19bb5fc8eeff2cc6df2682d3e9b188e01d9a7a00f79a48927", "source_text": "This article summarizes general structure results of Deligne-Mumford stacks (of finite type over a field) and contains some interesting results concerning quotient stacks. It is shown that any smooth, separated, generically tame Deligne-Mumford stack with quasi-projective coarse moduli space is a quotient stack <MATH_0001> with <MATH_0002> quasi-projective and <MATH_0003> an algebraic group. If <MATH_0004> is a Deligne-Mumford stack whose coarse moduli space is a scheme, then <MATH_0005> is Zariski-locally a quotient stack if and only if it admits a Zariski-open covering by stack quotients of schemes by finite groups. If <MATH_0006> is a Deligne-Mumford stack proper over a field of characteristic 0 with coarse moduli space <MATH_0007>, then: <MATH_0008> is projective and <MATH_0009> is a quotient stack if and only if <MATH_0010> is projective and <MATH_0011> possesses a generating sheaf if and only if <MATH_0012> admits a closed embedding into a smooth proper DM stack with projective coarse moduli space. This motivates a definition that a Deligne-Mumford stack is <EMPHOPEN_0001>projective<EMPHCLOSE_0001> if there exists a closed embedding into a smooth, proper Deligne-Mumford stack with projective coarse moduli space.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c6962eb9a5f2d4a8ebf43d40020da437a595bfa885ec5a67fba9c23b1b650d4e", "unit_id": "tag:04UZ:item004-quote"}
